ail":"R01"},{"week":10,"status":"RES","detail":"R01"}],"espn":{"summaryLabel":"2026 regular season stats","summary":[{"name":"soloTackles","label":"SOLO","value":"5","rank":"Tied-563rd"},{"name":"fumblesForced","label":"Forced Fumbles","value":"0","rank":"Tied-194th"},{"name":"interceptions","label":"Interceptions","value":"0","rank":"Tied-142nd"},{"name":"passesDefended","label":"Passes Defended","value":"2","rank":"Tied-181st"}],"birthPlace":"Detroit, MI","draftText":"2018: Rd 4, Pk 125 (PHI)"},"news":[{"headline":"Lions lose DB Avonte Maddox for season; Dan Campbell defends DC","description":"The embattled Lions defense has lost defensive back Avonte Maddox for the season, while coach Dan Campbell is defending second-year defensive coordinator Kelvin Sheppard.","published":"2026-09-21T20:57:56.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/49999325/lions-lose-db-avonte-maddox-season-dan-campbell-defends-dc","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Eric Woodyard","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Lions DB Avonte Maddox exits loss to Bills with foot injury","description":"Lions defensive back Avonte Maddox was ruled out Thursday night at Buffalo after injuring his foot in the second quarter.","published":"2026-09-18T04:52:56.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/49969456/lions-avonte-maddox-injures-foot-vs-bills-ruled-rest-game","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Eric Woodyard","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Lions 2025 free agency tracker: Offseason moves, signings","description":"Keep track of all the Lions' free agent moves throughout the 2025 offseason.","published":"2025-03-31T00:07:07.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/43923964/lions-2025-free-agency-tracker-offseason-moves-signings","type":"Story","byline":"Eric Woodyard","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Eagles put CB Avonte Maddox on IR with torn pectoral","description":"The Eagles placed slot cornerback Avonte Maddox on injured reserve Wednesday.","published":"2023-09-20T17:32:17.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/38446680/eagles-put-cb-avonte-maddox-ir-torn-pectoral","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Tim McManus","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Source: Eagles CB Avonte Maddox feared to have torn pectoral","description":"Eagles slot cornerback Avonte Maddox is feared to have torn a pectoral during Thursday night's win over the Minnesota Vikings, a source told ESPN's Adam Schefter.","published":"2023-09-15T19:46:07.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/38406833/source-eagles-cb-avonte-maddox-feared-torn-pectoral","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Tim McManus","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Stacking Super Bowl rosters: Eagles vs. Chiefs at 27 positions","description":"From Jalen Hurts vs. Patrick Mahomes at QB1 to Avonte Maddox vs. Jaylen Watson at CB3, we broke down which Super Bowl team has the advantage at 27 different positions.","published":"2023-10-12T17:41:45.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/insider/story/_/id/35616308/stacking-super-bowl-eagles-chiefs-rosters-edge-every-position-depth-chart-quarterback-receiver-cornerback","type":"Story","byline":"Matt Bowen","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Four things to monitor as Eagles move on from first loss of the season","description":"The Eagles' loss to the Commanders exposed several weaknesses, so how they adjust will be key.","published":"2022-11-18T12:43:17.000+00:00","url":"http://espn.com/blog/philadelphia-eagles/post/_/id/33305/four-things-to-monitor-as-eagles-move-on-from-first-loss-of-the-season","type":"BlogEntry","byline":"Tim McManus","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Eagles place CB Avonte Maddox (hamstring) on injured reserve","description":"The Eagles will be missing a key piece of their secondary for at least the next four weeks after placing starting slot corner Avonte Maddox on injured reserve Monday.","published":"2022-11-14T23:32:32.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/35028157/eagles-place-cb-avonte-maddox-hamstring-injured-reserve","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Tim McManus","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Dallas Goedert, Fletcher Cox among 12 Philadelphia Eagles players put on COVID-19 list Monday","description":"The Eagles placed 12 players on the reserve/COVID-19 list Monday.","published":"2022-01-03T22:35:14.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/32987365/dallas-goedert-fletcher-cox-12-eagles-put-covid-19-list-monday","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Tim McManus","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Philadelphia Eagles extend CB Avonte Maddox through 2024 season","description":"The Eagles have signed cornerback Avonte Maddox to a three-year extension through the 2024 season, the team announced.","published":"2021-11-20T17:30:53.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/32672794/sources-cb-avonte-maddox-agrees-3-year-225-million-extension-philadelphia-eagles","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"}],"wiki":{"title":"Avonte Maddox","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Avonte_Maddox","description":"American football player (born 1996)","touched":"2026-11-14T07:29:34Z","intro":"Avonte Michael Maddox (born March 31, 1996) is an American professional football safety for the Detroit Lions of the National Football League (NFL). He played college football for the Pittsburgh Panthers.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"After playing little league football, Maddox focused on baseball his first two years of high school before switching to football. He received only two Power Five scholarship offers, one from Purdue and one from Pittsburgh. He was also nearly drafted into the MLB after his senior year of high school."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"Maddox started at cornerback all four years at Pitt. He was named Honorable Mention All-Atlantic Coast Conference his sophomore year and Second-team his senior year. Maddox missed two games in both his junior and senior years due to injury.\n\nCOLLEGE STATISTICS"},{"key":"career","title":"Professional career","text":"PHILADELPHIA EAGLES\nMaddox was selected by the Philadelphia Eagles in the fourth round (125th overall) of the 2018 NFL draft. He made his NFL debut during the league season opener on September 6, 2018, against the Atlanta Falcons, playing on special teams. Maddox recorded his first career interception by picking off a pass from Tennessee Titans' quarterback Marcus Mariota in a 26–23 overtime loss on September 30. He recorded his second interception of the season off of quarterback Jared Goff during the 30–23 win over the Los Angeles Rams.\nOn September 26, 2019, late in a game against the Green Bay Packers, Maddox collided helmets with teammate Andrew Sendejo on an attempted tackle of Jamaal Williams and had to be carted off the field on a stretcher. The Eagles announced that Maddox had movement in all of his extremities, but was taken to a local hospital overnight as a precaution and for further evaluation; he returned with the team the next day.\nIn the 2020 season, during the Eagles' Week 3 game against the Cincinnati Bengals, Maddox suffered an injury which ultimately forced him to miss the next three games before being re-activated on Week 7. On December 18, 2020, Maddox was placed on season-ending injured reserve after suffering a knee injury in a Week 14 win over the New Orleans Saints. He finished the season with 40 tackles and three pass deflections, playing in 10 games with eight starts.\nStarting the last season of his rookie contract in 2021, Maddox led the Eagles in tackles (9) during their 32–6 win over the Atlanta Falcons. On October 24 against the Las Vegas Raiders, Maddox recorded his third career interception during the 33–22 loss. On November 20, 2021, Maddox signed a three-year, $22.5 million contract extension with the Eagles. He was placed on the COVID list on January 3, 2022. Maddox was activated one week later on January 10, missing just one game in which the Eagles did not use their starters.\nMaddox returned as a starter in 2022 as the team's primary nickelback. He was placed on injured reserve on November 14, 2022, with a hamstring injury. He was activated on December 10. On December 26, it was announced that Maddox had suffered a 'significant' toe injury and would miss the remainder of the regular season. Maddox reached Super Bowl LVII where the Eagles lost 38–35 to the Kansas City Chiefs; he recorded seven tackles in the game.\nOn September 20, 2023, Maddox was placed on injured reserve after suffering a pec injury in Week 2. He was activated on December 30.\nOn March 7, 2024, Maddox was released by the Eagles. He re-signed with the team on April 4. Maddox won his first Super Bowl when the Eagles defeated the Kansas City Chiefs 40–22 in Super Bowl LIX. Maddox had one pass defended in the game, forcing a turnover on downs.\n\nDETROIT LIONS\nOn March 21, 2025, Maddox signed a one-year contract with his hometown team, the Detroit Lions. \nOn April 6, 2026, Maddox signed another one-year contract with the Lions. In the Week 2 matchup against the Buffalo Bills, Maddox suffered a foot injury requiring season-ending surgery."}],"wikidataId":"Q52270732","social":{"x":"2live_am"}},"transactions":[{"date":"2026-09-22","text":"Released LB Joe Bachie. Signed DB Bishop Fitzgerald from Pittsburgh's practice squad. Placed DB Avonte Maddox on injured reserve."},{"date":"2026-04-06","text":"Signed DB Avonte Maddox to a contract."}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/3123938","pfr":"https://www.pro-football-reference.com/players/M/MaddAv00.htm","pff":"https://www.pff.com/nfl/players/avonte-maddox/50543","otc":"https://overthecap.com/player/avonte-maddox/7010","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Avonte_Maddox"},"insights":["On the field for 19% of Detroit’s defensive snaps this season.","2026 cap number of $1.3M is the 32nd-largest on the roster.","Contract expires after this season.","Drafted 125th overall in 2018 (round 4) by PHI."]}